```

So `X_STRIPE = 0x08`. The first byte `in[0]` must have bit 0x08 set. Then `var_get_u32` reads the ulen varint starting at `in[1]`. If all bytes from `in[1]` to `in[in_size-1]` have the high bit set (0x80), then `var_get_u32` reads all of them and returns `in_size - 1`. So `c_meta_len = 1 + (in_size - 1) = in_size`. Then `in[c_meta_len]` = `in[in_size]` reads 1 byte past the end of the buffer.

So the malicious data is:
- byte 0: 0x08 (X_STRIPE flag)
- bytes 1..n: all 0x80 (high bit set)

